  "findings": [
    "The official file has one row per farm (500 farms). The working copy used by the original notebook repeated every record 10 times (verified record-identical to the official file), so its row-level split placed identical copies in train and test.",
    "Coordinates do not match region labels: every region spans the same box (lat ~10-35, lon ~70-90 E). US regions would need negative longitudes; East Africa lies at lon ~28-52 E.",
    "All sowing dates fall in 2024-01-01 .. 2024-03-28 with the same window for every crop and region, although regional cropping calendars differ (e.g. Indian rice/cotton are usually sown in the monsoon season).",
    "10 of 11 numeric columns are statistically indistinguishable from a uniform distribution (KS p > 0.05).",
    "Largest |Pearson r| between any feature and yield is 0.077; no categorical column has an ANOVA p-value below 0.05 (min p = 0.180).",
    "Yield is ~Uniform(2000, 6000) kg/ha for every crop, including cotton, whose realistic yield scale differs from cereals.",
    "The publisher's description states the data 'simulates' smart-farming operations."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The data shows the signature of independently, uniformly generated columns with no built-in relationship to yield. Treat it as synthetic practice data, not field observations."
}